{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790465533,"nonce":"yuMfHm+IuGxy0IvmL03cBomtEj8=","title":"Python: function values, what P-func-values left unbuilt","message":"Module functions named as values are typed Ty::Func and calls through them are direct, reaching typed instances; methods named as values get instances for their typed calls. Not built:\n\n- FuncSet joins and escape tracking that would close a function passed only to in-view callees. Today a function named as a value keeps an Object generic; only instances are typed. A higher-order function passed two functions keeps an Object `func` in its generic (instances cover the typed sites, up to MAX_SPECS).\n- Bound methods passed as arguments typed as Bound sets (BoundInfo::Passed). In pyaes ECB, `block_func(block)` still calls through the bound$ record into the dynamic generic encrypt_block; CBC (the benchmark path) is typed through instances.\n- spectral-norm still boxes: part_*_times_u return Num (partial_sum starts as int 0), so eval_times_u lists are List(Object), and main's `u` joins List(Int) with List(Object) to Object. Steady state is ~21 ms/iteration on the NUC, far from the ~3 ms the design expects; no drop to LLVM within 20 iterations.","files":null}]}